WEBVTT

00:01.524 --> 00:04.402
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.910 --> 00:08.189
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.224 --> 00:11.772
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.806 --> 00:14.784
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:14.818 --> 00:18.298
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.333 --> 00:21.612
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.647 --> 00:23.186
♪ All the things that make us

00:23.220 --> 00:24.558
♪ Laugh and cry

00:24.593 --> 00:26.036
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.136 --> 00:36.542
TV ANNOUNCER:
We now return to

00:36.576 --> 00:39.688
<i>11 Angry Men and One
Developmentally Disabled Man.</i>

00:39.723 --> 00:41.796
Okay, the vote is
11 for "guilty"

00:41.831 --> 00:43.370
and one for "kitty."

00:43.405 --> 00:44.575
(all groaning)

00:44.609 --> 00:46.617
All right,
let's keep talking it out...

00:48.325 --> 00:50.098
Has the jury
reached its verdict?

00:50.133 --> 00:51.304
We have, Your Honor.

00:51.338 --> 00:52.977
We find the defendant...
kitty.

00:53.011 --> 00:54.918
(gallery shouting, murmuring)

00:58.635 --> 01:00.710
Boy, am I beat.

01:00.744 --> 01:02.115
Peter, what's
with the tie?

01:02.149 --> 01:04.425
Oh, I bought a tie so I can
loosen it when I'm beat.

01:04.460 --> 01:05.429
(sighs heavily)

01:05.464 --> 01:06.433
(exclaiming)

01:06.468 --> 01:07.805
Oh, my God, Dad!

01:07.840 --> 01:09.646
Peter, your breath!
It's horrible.

01:09.681 --> 01:10.752
(sniffs)

01:10.786 --> 01:13.094
Is Whoopi Goldberg
working out down there?

01:13.129 --> 01:14.835
Peter, I think
what everyone's saying

01:14.870 --> 01:16.307
is that you've
got "dad breath."

01:16.343 --> 01:17.747
What the hell's
"dad breath"?

01:17.782 --> 01:18.886
You know,
"dad breath."

01:18.920 --> 01:19.956
Guys get older,

01:19.991 --> 01:21.476
they stop paying
attention to hygiene,

01:21.497 --> 01:23.203
their bodies
are changing...

01:23.237 --> 01:25.078
It's just a fact that,
at a certain age,

01:25.112 --> 01:27.321
men start to rot
from the inside out.

01:27.355 --> 01:28.559
(exhales, sniffs)

01:28.594 --> 01:29.898
I don't smell it.

01:29.933 --> 01:31.204
Huh. Maybe that
explains what happened

01:31.238 --> 01:32.978
with that new guy
at work today.

01:33.046 --> 01:34.585
All right, so this
is Pawtucket Patriot's

01:34.619 --> 01:35.923
national distribution.

01:35.958 --> 01:37.129
As you can see,

01:37.163 --> 01:39.003
we are predominantly
an East Coast beer.

01:39.037 --> 01:40.676
Hey, there's gonna be a quiz
on all this later.

01:40.711 --> 01:41.948
I'm just kidding.

01:41.983 --> 01:43.220
Someone said that
to me once,

01:43.255 --> 01:44.526
now I say it.

01:50.184 --> 01:51.823
Hey, Lois,
what do you say

01:51.858 --> 01:53.798
we do what Anderson
Cooper tried once

01:53.832 --> 01:55.606
before he decided
he hated it?

01:55.640 --> 01:57.514
Oh, Peter...

01:57.548 --> 01:58.518
Hi, there.

01:58.552 --> 01:59.890
Ugh. Oh.

01:59.924 --> 02:01.095
Let's do some
role-playing.

02:01.129 --> 02:02.535
You're you
and I'm Peter,

02:02.569 --> 02:03.672
only with
much worse knees.

02:03.708 --> 02:05.012
Ow, my knees!

02:05.046 --> 02:06.484
Actually, Peter,

02:06.518 --> 02:08.259
I think I finally
want to make love

02:08.293 --> 02:10.669
to a 1950's spaceman.

02:10.703 --> 02:12.476
Really? You mean it?!

02:12.511 --> 02:13.514
All right, let's go!

02:17.732 --> 02:19.506
Good.

02:22.988 --> 02:26.233
Ugh, Dad, it smells like
rotting flesh in here.

02:26.268 --> 02:27.405
Take the window lock off!

02:27.440 --> 02:28.677
Can't do that, Meg.

02:28.712 --> 02:31.121
I don't trust myself
not to jump out the window.

02:31.155 --> 02:33.029
♪ But Minnie had a heart

02:33.063 --> 02:34.401
Ah, now this
is music.

02:34.435 --> 02:35.907
♪ As big as a whale

02:35.942 --> 02:38.117
♪ Hidee hidee hidee hi

02:38.151 --> 02:40.359
♪ Hidee hidee
hidee hi ♪

02:40.394 --> 02:42.669
(over radio):
♪ Hodee hodee hodee ho

02:42.704 --> 02:45.180
♪ Hodee hodee
hodee ho ♪

02:45.214 --> 02:47.556
(over radio):
♪ Heedee heedee heedee hee

02:47.590 --> 02:49.866
♪ Heedee heedee
heedee hee ♪

02:49.901 --> 02:51.406
(sobbing)

02:52.445 --> 02:53.481
(tires screech)

02:53.515 --> 02:55.255
Oh, my God!
Meg, are you okay?

02:55.290 --> 02:57.197
Do you need mouth-to-nose
resuscitation?

02:57.231 --> 02:57.899
(Peter inhales)

02:57.934 --> 02:59.674
(Meg screaming)

03:04.193 --> 03:06.603
(sighs):
Ah... politics.

03:06.637 --> 03:09.113
(disgusted groan)

03:09.147 --> 03:11.121
(sighs): Ah...
coach is a bum.

03:11.156 --> 03:13.130
(groans):
Oh, bloody hell!

03:13.164 --> 03:14.469
Heh! Beetle Bailey.

03:14.503 --> 03:16.109
Heh! Ha-ha! Ha!

03:16.143 --> 03:17.783
Ha-ha-ha!
Oh, that's it!

03:17.817 --> 03:20.192
All right, fat man,
two can play at that game.

03:20.227 --> 03:21.298
(strained grunting)

03:21.332 --> 03:22.536
(farts)

03:22.571 --> 03:24.109
Aah! Friendly fire!

03:24.144 --> 03:25.548
All right,
that's it, Peter,

03:25.584 --> 03:27.792
we've got to do something
about that awful breath.

03:27.826 --> 03:28.996
I'm making an appointment,

03:29.031 --> 03:30.604
and you are going
to the dentist.

03:30.638 --> 03:33.114
Geez, you are not gonna
let this go, are you?

03:33.148 --> 03:35.490
You're as stubborn as
a four-hour erection.

03:35.524 --> 03:38.737
<i>Well, she's long gone,
so, uh, you can go, too.</i>

03:38.772 --> 03:40.043
MALE VOICE:
Oh, no,

03:40.077 --> 03:41.616
you got me for another
three and half hours, pal.

03:41.651 --> 03:43.189
Go ahead,
seek medical attention.

03:43.224 --> 03:45.197
I'm not going anywhere.
You can't stay!

03:45.232 --> 03:46.403
I'm chaperoning
my daughter's

03:46.437 --> 03:47.775
Girl Scout dinner
in 45 minutes!

03:47.809 --> 03:49.314
Well, tuck me
into your waistband

03:49.349 --> 03:51.424
and try not to pee
up your shirt.

03:56.612 --> 03:57.683
Oh, boy.

03:57.718 --> 03:59.859
All right, I think
I found the culprit.

03:59.893 --> 04:02.336
This shrimp was lodged
under one of your gums.

04:02.370 --> 04:04.444
Wow, that must've been
in there a while.

04:04.480 --> 04:07.156
It's been weeks since I ordered
from Hurry Up, Shrimp.

04:07.190 --> 04:08.997
(sighs)
Where the hell is this guy?

04:09.031 --> 04:10.905
I ordered that shrimp
two hours ago.

04:10.939 --> 04:12.144
<i>MALE ANNOUNCER:
Uh-oh!</i>

04:12.178 --> 04:13.282
<i>Looks like
you should've ordered</i>

04:13.316 --> 04:14.721
<i>from Hurry Up, Shrimp.</i>

04:14.755 --> 04:17.667
<i>Hurry Up, Shrimp?
Well, that just sounds fast.</i>

04:17.701 --> 04:20.178
On average, Americans spend
upwards of 50,000 hours

04:20.212 --> 04:22.654
waiting for shrimp
over the course of their lives.

04:22.689 --> 04:24.897
When I heard that,
I thought to myself,

04:24.932 --> 04:27.408
"Why on earth don't
these guys just hurry up?"

04:27.442 --> 04:29.482
So that's just what we did.

04:30.522 --> 04:31.658
(tires screech)

04:31.693 --> 04:33.499
Come on! Come on!

04:33.534 --> 04:35.742
MAN: No way
this is the shrimp.

04:35.776 --> 04:37.450
Wow, it is!

04:37.484 --> 04:39.190
♪ Hurry Up, Shrimp,
Hurry up, Shrimp ♪

04:39.224 --> 04:41.399
♪ Hurry Up, Hurry Up,
Hurry Up, Shrimp. ♪

04:49.367 --> 04:51.140
Well, I'm very proud
of you, Peter.

04:51.174 --> 04:53.650
And since you were so well
behaved at the dentist,

04:53.685 --> 04:55.659
you can order
anything you want.

04:55.694 --> 04:58.002
<i>Oh, Dad, when do I get
to go to the dentist?</i>

04:58.036 --> 04:59.408
When you're older, Chris.

04:59.443 --> 05:01.115
Good evening,
countrymen.

05:01.149 --> 05:03.291
And women.
(giggles): Oh!

05:03.325 --> 05:05.333
Welcome to
The Founding Father.

05:05.368 --> 05:07.040
Hey, little guy.

05:07.074 --> 05:10.421
You know, that's a real treasure map
you've got there.

05:10.455 --> 05:13.768
Okay, well, I guess treasure
hunting isn't for everyone.

05:13.803 --> 05:15.207
Treasure, you say?

05:15.242 --> 05:17.550
Ah, yes.
You see, legend has it

05:17.585 --> 05:19.860
that Quahog founder
Miles "Chatterbox" Musket

05:19.895 --> 05:22.605
hid his fortune
in fear of it being taken

05:22.640 --> 05:25.015
by British soldiers
during the Revolutionary War.

05:25.049 --> 05:27.191
He died before
he could retrieve it,

05:27.225 --> 05:29.366
and left behind only this map.

05:29.401 --> 05:31.743
Many believe his treasure
is still buried

05:31.778 --> 05:33.818
right here in Rhode Island.

05:37.903 --> 05:40.146
Okay, I'm gonna
go do diarrhea,

05:40.180 --> 05:43.292
and then I'll be right back
to take your order.

05:44.330 --> 05:46.036
Lois, I know where this is!

05:46.070 --> 05:48.045
Peter, please,
that's just a place mat

05:48.079 --> 05:50.053
to distract your children
while you're eating.

05:50.087 --> 05:52.196
There's no treasure.
Well, what if there is?

05:52.230 --> 05:53.970
Ah, see?
Surprised you with that one.

05:54.004 --> 05:56.078
You see, you see that rock
next to the "X"?

05:56.112 --> 05:58.522
I know that rock, Lois--
it's right near Route 2.

05:58.556 --> 06:01.200
I'm finding that treasure.
Peter, the map is a joke.

06:01.235 --> 06:02.873
You're being played
for a fool.

06:02.908 --> 06:04.648
Like George McFly.

06:04.682 --> 06:06.053
Hey, Lorraine,

06:06.088 --> 06:08.296
whatever happened to that guy
Marty from high school?

06:08.330 --> 06:10.338
Don't know.
Never saw him after the prom.

06:10.373 --> 06:11.835
Really? Sure you didn't

06:11.860 --> 06:14.055
run into him, oh, say,
about 16 years ago?

06:14.456 --> 06:16.363
George, what are
you talking about?

06:16.397 --> 06:18.505
I'm talking about
the fact that our son,

06:18.540 --> 06:20.915
who you insisted we name
after that guy Marty,

06:20.950 --> 06:22.288
looks exactly like him!

06:22.322 --> 06:24.497
You think I'm an idiot?
That I wouldn't notice

06:24.531 --> 06:27.878
that our son is a dead ringer
for the guy who fixed us up?

06:27.912 --> 06:30.991
Mom, Dad, I accidentally set
fire to the living room rug!

06:31.025 --> 06:33.300
I am not going easy on him!

06:37.452 --> 06:40.329
Hey, guys, who wants to dig
for buried treasure with me?

06:40.364 --> 06:42.070
What? What are you
talking about?

06:42.105 --> 06:43.577
Well, this child's
place mat is telling me

06:43.611 --> 06:45.317
to dig for buried treasure
by the side of the highway.

06:45.351 --> 06:46.723
Who's in?

06:46.758 --> 06:48.397
Aw, forget it, Peter.
That's crazy talk.

06:48.431 --> 06:51.142
Yeah, we're not going along
with another one of your stupid ideas.

06:51.176 --> 06:52.615
I don't have
stupid ideas.

06:52.649 --> 06:54.858
Haven't you seen my
documentary film?

06:54.892 --> 06:57.267
<i>PETER: Each year,
the environment covers</i>

06:57.301 --> 06:59.879
<i>more than 40% of the Earth.</i>

06:59.913 --> 07:03.460
<i>Every animal on Earth
lays eggs.</i>

07:03.494 --> 07:05.167
<i>This is a birch tree.</i>

07:05.202 --> 07:09.451
<i>Today it will begin
its 10,000-mile journey.</i>

07:09.486 --> 07:12.163
<i>The Earth neither
hates nor loves,</i>

07:12.197 --> 07:16.816
<i>but sits, waiting patiently,
for people to do famous stuff.</i>

07:23.445 --> 07:25.251
Peter, it's time
to come home.

07:25.286 --> 07:27.159
You been out here
digging all day.

07:27.194 --> 07:29.903
I-I told you this whole thing
was ridiculous.

07:29.939 --> 07:31.678
What the hell was
I thinking, anyway?

07:31.712 --> 07:33.386
I must be some
kind of idiot.

07:33.420 --> 07:34.423
(shovel clangs)

07:34.457 --> 07:36.632
(gasps)
(gasps) What was that?

07:38.674 --> 07:41.519
Holy crap!
Lois, it's the treasure!

07:41.554 --> 07:42.825
Oh, my God!

07:42.859 --> 07:45.068
Peter, you were right!

07:45.102 --> 07:46.808
Oh, no, it's the one kid

07:46.842 --> 07:48.414
who also followed
the treasure map.

07:59.614 --> 08:00.718
I don't believe it!

08:00.752 --> 08:02.726
There really was something
buried out there!

08:02.760 --> 08:05.035
Well, it's not the treasure,
but it looks like

08:05.071 --> 08:07.044
it's a clue
to where the treasure is.

08:07.079 --> 08:09.086
"Face the circle
in the square,

08:09.120 --> 08:11.463
you'll see me,
I'll show you where."

08:11.497 --> 08:13.103
Interesting.

08:13.137 --> 08:15.814
Interesting, interesting.

08:22.008 --> 08:23.773
Okay, well, if there is
a treasure out there,

08:23.782 --> 08:25.454
we don't want anybody else
to know about it.

08:25.489 --> 08:26.803
None of this leaves
this room, okay?

08:26.828 --> 08:27.630
Obviously.

08:27.631 --> 08:29.003
We're not idiots, Brian.

08:29.037 --> 08:31.078
Hey, look!
Dad's on TV!

08:31.113 --> 08:32.417
Hello, I'm Tom Tucker,

08:32.452 --> 08:34.525
here with local fortune seeker
Peter Griffin, who appears

08:34.561 --> 08:36.802
to have found a clue
to a hidden treasure.

08:36.837 --> 08:38.108
That's right, Tom,
and I sincerely hope

08:38.142 --> 08:39.949
that the caption beneath me

08:39.983 --> 08:42.593
doesn't say "Local Fatty."
Let's do something about that caption.

08:42.627 --> 08:45.606
All right, well, you can check
out the clue at our Web site:

08:49.624 --> 08:51.965
We were a little late
getting a Web site.

08:52.000 --> 08:54.075
Quick, Neil! Sign into
the neighbors' Wi-Fi

08:54.109 --> 08:55.916
so we can get that clue.

08:55.950 --> 08:56.979
Nurse, write down that clue,

08:57.004 --> 08:59.230
and then go out in
the waiting room and...

08:59.330 --> 09:01.505
maybe start lowering
expectations.

09:01.540 --> 09:02.610
Treasure?!

09:02.644 --> 09:03.714
Yeah, baby?

09:03.750 --> 09:05.723
Bring me a grape wine.

09:05.758 --> 09:06.761
Peter, what the hell!

09:06.795 --> 09:07.899
Now everyone has the clue!

09:07.933 --> 09:09.171
Why would you do that?

09:09.205 --> 09:10.530
Because I'm tired
of people saying

09:10.544 --> 09:12.049
I don't know nothin'.
Everyone doubted me,

09:12.084 --> 09:14.895
so I wanted to rub it
in their faces that I was right.

09:14.929 --> 09:15.899
All right, where is it?

09:15.933 --> 09:17.573
Give me that!
Is this all there was?

09:17.607 --> 09:18.744
Yeah, is there
anything else

09:18.778 --> 09:20.351
we should know before
we start looking?

09:20.386 --> 09:22.091
<i>Whoa, whoa, whoa.
This is our thing.</i>

09:22.126 --> 09:23.565
We're not sharing
this with anyone.

09:23.599 --> 09:25.071
Peter, come on,
are you serious?

09:25.105 --> 09:27.883
If Joe or I found this, we'd
want you right alongside us.

09:27.917 --> 09:30.125
Well, yeah, we're
like peas in a pod.

09:30.160 --> 09:31.967
Wait-wait.
Don't go in there.

09:32.001 --> 09:34.108
He's doing his podcast.

09:34.142 --> 09:35.113
Oh, that's cute.

09:35.147 --> 09:37.523
<i>Now, that I like.</i>

09:37.557 --> 09:39.698
<i>What do you think about this,
you old bag?</i>

09:39.733 --> 09:42.042
Oh, no.

09:42.076 --> 09:44.117
Look, you guys
doubted me, mocked me,

09:44.151 --> 09:46.259
constantly handled my Eggo
despite my clear instructions,

09:46.294 --> 09:48.535
and now you want a
piece of my treasure?

09:48.570 --> 09:49.344
I don't think so.

09:49.369 --> 09:51.070
Well, fine!
We don't need you anyway!

09:52.520 --> 09:54.125
Peter, I don't like this.

09:54.160 --> 09:55.431
It seems like this treasure

09:55.465 --> 09:57.037
is already turning people
against each other.

09:57.073 --> 09:58.242
Hang on, you guys.

09:58.277 --> 10:00.050
I think I might have
figured something out.

10:00.085 --> 10:01.724
"The circle in the square."

10:01.759 --> 10:04.101
That could be the clock
in the town square.

10:04.135 --> 10:06.511
Wow, that... You're right!
Brian, that could be it!

10:06.545 --> 10:08.653
Well, let's get down there
before anyone else does.

10:13.776 --> 10:17.088
(townspeople murmuring)

10:17.122 --> 10:19.365
Son of a bitch!
Everyone's already here!

10:19.399 --> 10:22.377
Let's see, "Face
the circle in the square."

10:22.411 --> 10:24.386
"Face the circle."

10:24.420 --> 10:25.590
"Face."

10:25.625 --> 10:27.465
Okay, the gesturing
needs to stop.

10:27.500 --> 10:29.072
No one else is doing that.

10:33.056 --> 10:34.996
Look!
When you face this way,

10:35.031 --> 10:37.976
you're looking at
the statue of Miles Musket.

10:39.751 --> 10:41.725
Crap, you guys, there's
already other people here.

10:41.759 --> 10:43.499
They must have
figured it out, too.

10:43.534 --> 10:45.139
You're right.
Okay, gather round, kids.

10:45.174 --> 10:46.177
Family suicide.

10:46.211 --> 10:47.583
Look-- there's a plaque!

10:47.617 --> 10:50.227
"This square
shall forever honor

10:50.261 --> 10:51.934
"the memory of my son,
Timmy Musket.

10:51.969 --> 10:54.144
"Always a chip
off the old Block.

10:54.178 --> 10:55.649
"May he rest in peace.

10:55.684 --> 10:57.692
Miles 'Chatterbox' Musket."

10:57.726 --> 11:00.570
Wait-- when I played Jane Musket
in the school play

11:00.605 --> 11:02.345
the last three weekends--
thanks for coming...

11:02.379 --> 11:03.850
I couldn't.
I had a thing.

11:03.886 --> 11:05.826
I had a lot of
dog stuff that day.

11:05.860 --> 11:07.867
Yeah, weekends I like
to spend with my kids.

11:07.902 --> 11:09.708
I learned that
Timmy Musket is buried

11:09.743 --> 11:11.348
in a cemetery
on Block Island.

11:11.383 --> 11:13.256
I remember it because
my big speech was, "Timmy..."

11:13.292 --> 11:14.562
Meg, please.

11:14.597 --> 11:16.637
That must be what "chip off
the old Block" means!

11:16.672 --> 11:18.412
That's it!
Meg, take the car home!

11:18.446 --> 11:21.223
Your mother and I are taking
the ferry to Block Island!

11:21.258 --> 11:23.265
Chris, we need to find that
treasure for ourselves.

11:23.299 --> 11:24.503
What do you mean?

11:24.538 --> 11:26.010
<i>Even if Dad finds
the treasure,</i>

11:26.044 --> 11:27.082
he's not gonna share.

11:27.116 --> 11:28.420
He'll just blow
through it all.

11:28.455 --> 11:29.524
Maybe you're right.

11:29.559 --> 11:31.432
I mean, last time
we came into some money,

11:31.467 --> 11:32.805
he just wasted it
on all those

11:32.840 --> 11:33.976
diamond pinkie rings
for everybody.

11:34.012 --> 11:35.181
What?!

11:35.216 --> 11:37.658
Uh, well, uh, yeah,
we should probably go.

11:39.869 --> 11:40.906
(tires screeching)

11:40.940 --> 11:42.513
What the hell?
Where are they going?

11:42.547 --> 11:43.718
Oh, forget them.
They're dead weight.

11:43.752 --> 11:45.157
If this treasure's going
to be found,

11:45.191 --> 11:46.630
it's up to you
and me, Brian.

11:46.664 --> 11:48.403
What do you mean?
Come on! You think

11:48.439 --> 11:50.124
the fat man's gonna
figure out those clues?

11:50.145 --> 11:52.086
He's an idiot.
Yeah, I guess you're right.

11:52.120 --> 11:53.424
Yes, I mean,
he's the guy

11:53.460 --> 11:55.467
who put all those
little bald men in incubators

11:55.501 --> 11:56.839
because he thought
they were babies.

11:56.873 --> 11:58.480
Look at you.

11:58.514 --> 12:00.789
You came early,
but you're gonna make it.

12:00.823 --> 12:03.567
I'm a senior vice president
at an investment firm!

12:03.602 --> 12:06.513
Oh, someone's a fussy britches.

12:22.012 --> 12:24.387
♪ Sailing

12:24.422 --> 12:26.463
♪ Takes me away

12:26.497 --> 12:28.572
♪ To where I've always

12:28.607 --> 12:30.948
♪ Heard it could be...

12:35.133 --> 12:36.806
Want half a Mounds bar?

12:36.841 --> 12:38.178
What?

12:38.213 --> 12:39.551
Who eats a Mounds bar?

12:39.586 --> 12:41.526
I do.
My whole life, I don't think

12:41.560 --> 12:43.702
I've ever seen a single
person eat a Mounds bar.

12:43.736 --> 12:45.643
Well, you're about
to see one now.

12:45.678 --> 12:47.015
So, you walk
into a store,

12:47.050 --> 12:48.696
you see the hundreds
of options for candy,

12:48.724 --> 12:50.229
and you choose
a Mounds bar?

12:50.264 --> 12:51.334
Yep.

12:51.368 --> 12:52.873
So what is it you like?

12:52.908 --> 12:53.911
The coconut?
The chocolate?

12:53.945 --> 12:55.083
Yeah.
Both those things.

12:55.117 --> 12:56.388
How long you been
eating 'em?

12:56.422 --> 12:58.028
Uh, I've probably
been having a Mounds bar

12:58.063 --> 13:00.305
two or three times a day
for the last 25 years.

13:00.339 --> 13:01.978
Geez, no wonder
you can't walk!

13:02.012 --> 13:03.953
You have total
renal shutdown!

13:03.987 --> 13:05.292
Your kidneys are
drowning in a stew

13:05.327 --> 13:06.463
of chocolate and coconut!

13:06.498 --> 13:07.502
Give me that!

13:10.415 --> 13:11.719
(candy wrapper crinkling)

13:11.753 --> 13:13.292
What are you doing?

13:15.737 --> 13:18.346
Why are your nipples
poking into me?

13:18.381 --> 13:20.622
Sorry. That happens
when I'm cold.

13:20.658 --> 13:22.464
But why are there
three of them?

13:22.498 --> 13:23.267
There aren't.

13:23.302 --> 13:24.673
Two of them are moles.

13:24.707 --> 13:27.150
Those numbers
still don't add up!

13:30.197 --> 13:32.171
Why the hell are we taking
a hot air balloon?

13:32.205 --> 13:34.247
I don't think we're anywhere
near Block Island.

13:34.281 --> 13:36.054
Oh, I know.
We passed that miles ago.

13:36.089 --> 13:38.230
What? Well, then what
about the treasure?

13:38.265 --> 13:41.377
Two friends sailing in
the sky in a wicker basket

13:41.411 --> 13:43.854
with a strange man
holding a cheese plate?

13:43.888 --> 13:45.594
This is the treasure, Bri.

13:45.628 --> 13:47.167
You want a Vicodin?

13:47.201 --> 13:50.079
Isn't it dangerous to do drugs
10,000 feet in the air?

13:50.113 --> 13:52.088
Yeah. Exactly.

13:52.122 --> 13:53.293
What the hell?!

13:53.328 --> 13:55.335
Never gonna die!

13:55.369 --> 13:57.076
Your friend is, like,
the coolest guy

13:57.110 --> 13:58.849
I've ever had up here.

14:01.260 --> 14:03.167
Oh, damn it, Lois,
they're already here!

14:03.202 --> 14:04.741
This is all your fault!

14:04.743 --> 14:06.280
What?! How is this my fault?

14:06.315 --> 14:08.423
Because you just had
to stop for ice cream!

14:08.457 --> 14:10.331
Then you get in there,
and you order

14:10.365 --> 14:12.038
like you never
heard of food before!

14:12.072 --> 14:15.988
Oh, "Coffee Fudge Swirl with
Reese's Peanut Butter Cups."

14:16.022 --> 14:18.097
Oh, I wonder
what's in that!

14:18.131 --> 14:20.273
You just listed off
all the ingredients!

14:20.307 --> 14:22.983
Everything you just said
is what's in that!

14:24.993 --> 14:26.900
Well, I hate to say it,
but I guess

14:26.935 --> 14:28.407
we're supposed
to dig this kid up.

14:28.441 --> 14:29.645
Any volunteers?

14:29.680 --> 14:31.452
I dig kids.

14:31.487 --> 14:32.691
All of you,
hold it right there!

14:32.725 --> 14:33.896
If anyone's digging

14:33.930 --> 14:35.101
into this little kid's grave,
it's me!

14:35.136 --> 14:36.741
You're too late.
We got here first.

14:36.776 --> 14:37.946
No, it's my treasure hunt!

14:37.981 --> 14:39.118
I found the first clue!

14:39.153 --> 14:40.490
You guys are just horning in!

14:40.525 --> 14:41.662
You guys, calm down!

14:41.696 --> 14:43.537
See, this is what
I was talking about.

14:43.571 --> 14:44.975
You can't desecrate
a child's grave!

14:44.976 --> 14:46.114
Don't worry, Lois.

14:46.148 --> 14:47.519
We're gonna do it
with reverence.

14:47.555 --> 14:49.227
Hey, how about
a little digging song?

14:49.261 --> 14:51.503
(to "Little Bunny Foo Foo"):
♪ Little Peter Griffin

14:51.537 --> 14:52.842
♪ Diggin' up a casket

14:52.877 --> 14:56.390
♪ Shovelful of dirt
and bop ya on the head. ♪

14:56.425 --> 14:58.298
I didn't care for
the end of that song.

14:58.333 --> 15:00.441
Oh, my God!
The treasure's in the casket!

15:00.475 --> 15:02.650
Come on, Meg,
let's get it!

15:02.684 --> 15:03.889
My treasure!

15:03.923 --> 15:06.432
Oh, my God!
You hit your own son!

15:06.467 --> 15:07.704
That's it, Peter.

15:07.739 --> 15:10.817
I am not gonna stand here
and be a part of this madness.

15:10.852 --> 15:13.060
You're on your own,
because I quit!

15:13.094 --> 15:14.700
Chris, Meg,
we're going home.

15:14.734 --> 15:17.545
Well, good! You were just
slowing me down anyway!

15:17.579 --> 15:19.855
You, Asian lady,
you're the new Lois.

15:19.890 --> 15:24.206
I will have one scoop of mint
chocolate chip in a waffle cone.

15:24.241 --> 15:26.751
You are a practical,
straightforward people.

15:32.000 --> 15:33.575
What do you guys think
is in here?

15:33.576 --> 15:34.480
(rattling)

15:34.481 --> 15:35.953
Sounds like books.

15:36.858 --> 15:38.162
(all gasping)

15:38.196 --> 15:40.639
BRUCE:
Oh, my God!

15:40.673 --> 15:42.982
Feels so weird to be
looking at a dead kid

15:43.016 --> 15:44.588
and not have angry
parents nearby.

15:44.624 --> 15:47.869
Hey, look! There's something
written inside the lid.

15:47.904 --> 15:50.949
PETER: "You've crossed the miles,
you've pawed through clues.

15:50.983 --> 15:54.999
Find where he hits, misses,
cheers and boos."

15:55.034 --> 15:57.342
By the way, for those
who came on my boat,

15:57.376 --> 15:58.949
I have those
sandwiches.

15:58.983 --> 16:01.827
"Hits, misses,
cheers, and boos."

16:01.861 --> 16:03.602
Could be... baseball?

16:03.636 --> 16:05.208
And "pawed through clues."

16:05.242 --> 16:07.384
Could it be Paw... tucket?

16:07.418 --> 16:09.961
The Pawtucket Red Sox play
at McCoy Stadium.

16:09.996 --> 16:12.305
Quagmire, let's get
to that stadium!

16:16.691 --> 16:18.062
Eh! Lois took the bike.

16:18.096 --> 16:19.502
Hey, wait a minute.

16:19.536 --> 16:23.050
This is a great time for me
to do my Suzuki Samurai promo!

16:24.757 --> 16:26.732
Are you a Hawaii scumbag?

16:26.766 --> 16:29.209
Do you chug energy drinks
in Arizona?

16:29.243 --> 16:33.594
Suzuki Samurai--
ninja name, garbage car.

16:37.444 --> 16:39.552
You sons of bitches,
this is my...

16:39.587 --> 16:41.594
(yelling, grunting
and muttering)

16:44.608 --> 16:46.548
Oh, my God, look at 'em.

16:46.582 --> 16:48.054
Lois was right.

16:48.089 --> 16:51.066
This treasure hunt has
turned them all into animals.

16:51.101 --> 16:52.305
(grunting)

16:52.339 --> 16:54.146
There's more
where that came from, mister!

16:54.181 --> 16:55.318
(grunts)

16:55.352 --> 16:57.795
<i>He was right.
There was more!</i>

17:01.980 --> 17:04.456
Oh, look who's back--
the grave robber.

17:04.490 --> 17:05.728
Hey, Lois.

17:05.762 --> 17:08.138
So, what happened?
You find your treasure?

17:08.173 --> 17:10.884
No. I realized something
after you left.

17:10.918 --> 17:12.892
It's not the treasure
that matters.

17:12.926 --> 17:15.201
All that really matters
is the money you get

17:15.235 --> 17:17.142
<i>in exchange
for the treasure.</i>

17:17.177 --> 17:19.486
I guess I had
to learn that the hard way.

17:19.520 --> 17:21.561
Per, you were a real jerk
out there!

17:21.596 --> 17:22.833
I know.

17:22.868 --> 17:23.804
You were right.

17:23.838 --> 17:25.477
I took this thing way too far.

17:25.512 --> 17:28.156
And I'm really sorry about
how I treated you and the kids.

17:28.190 --> 17:29.327
But you know me.

17:29.361 --> 17:31.269
If I read anything
on a place mat,

17:31.303 --> 17:32.708
I I just kind of go nuts.

17:32.742 --> 17:34.114
Can you forgive me?

17:34.148 --> 17:35.419
Chris forgave me.

17:35.454 --> 17:38.800
I can't wait for you
to fall asleep tonight.

17:38.835 --> 17:40.842
Of course I
forgive you, Peter.

17:40.876 --> 17:43.955
So I guess everyone else came
to their senses, too, huh?

17:43.989 --> 17:45.929
No, they all ran off
to McCoy Stadium.

17:45.964 --> 17:48.005
What? Why? What's
at McCoy Stadium?

17:48.040 --> 17:50.047
Ah, there was a clue
at the graveyard.

17:50.081 --> 17:51.921
Here, I took a picture
with my phone.

17:51.955 --> 17:53.595
Oh, it's the
next picture.

17:53.630 --> 17:56.474
Just swipe it
to the next one.

17:58.249 --> 18:00.223
She saw me.

18:00.257 --> 18:03.168
"You've crossed the miles,
you've pawed through clues.

18:03.203 --> 18:06.984
Find where he hits,
misses, cheers and boos."

18:07.018 --> 18:10.265
Peter, this can't be leading
them to a baseball stadium.

18:10.299 --> 18:13.077
Baseball wasn't invented
until the 1800s.

18:13.111 --> 18:15.353
Wow, you're really smart, Lois.

18:15.387 --> 18:17.529
You know, Peter,
in the first eight minutes

18:17.563 --> 18:19.370
of Meg's play,
before I walked out,

18:19.404 --> 18:22.182
they said Miles Musket
was a horrible drunk

18:22.216 --> 18:23.487
and a wife beater.

18:23.521 --> 18:25.328
So, when it says,
"hits, misses,"

18:25.362 --> 18:28.575
it might be talking
about hitting Mrs. Musket.

18:28.609 --> 18:30.516
And he probably misspelled
"missus"

18:30.551 --> 18:32.525
because he was drunk
when he wrote it.

18:32.559 --> 18:34.767
Or maybe he misspelled it
because cursive is hard,

18:34.802 --> 18:36.507
and everyone should
get off his back.

18:36.543 --> 18:39.119
And "cheers" and "boos"
might be referring to a bar

18:39.153 --> 18:41.998
where he would "cheers,"
and drink his "booze."

18:42.032 --> 18:44.541
"Hits missus,
cheers and booze."

18:44.576 --> 18:46.751
Wait a minute-- it's got
to be an old bar, right?

18:46.785 --> 18:48.458
The Clam's
the oldest bar in town.

18:48.493 --> 18:50.668
(gasps) That must be
where the treasure is!

18:50.702 --> 18:52.642
All right, let's you
put some makeup on

18:52.677 --> 18:54.417
and get right down
to The Clam!

18:56.961 --> 18:59.939
Oh, no, they're closed.

18:59.973 --> 19:01.647
Hang on. I got an idea.

19:01.681 --> 19:03.086
But you have to believe.

19:03.120 --> 19:04.893
What?
You have to believe.

19:04.928 --> 19:06.099
Say you believe.

19:06.133 --> 19:07.705
Okay. I believe.

19:07.740 --> 19:11.053
This is worse than the time
we were in The Clam right now.

19:11.087 --> 19:12.558
Yes!

19:12.594 --> 19:13.697
Peter, look!

19:13.731 --> 19:15.705
That's Miles Musket!

19:15.740 --> 19:17.312
It is?
Yes!

19:17.347 --> 19:19.655
How have you never seen
this painting before?

19:19.689 --> 19:22.266
Lois, I'm completely hammered
every time I'm in here.

19:26.250 --> 19:27.187
(grunts)

19:33.447 --> 19:34.751
(both gasp)

19:35.790 --> 19:37.362
We did it!

19:37.397 --> 19:39.371
We found the treasure!

19:39.405 --> 19:40.710
You know what, Peter?

19:40.744 --> 19:42.719
<i>Why don't you open it?</i>

19:42.753 --> 19:44.727
Oh, yeah.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

19:44.761 --> 19:47.069
No, okay,
I'll-I'll open it.

19:47.105 --> 19:50.016
Here, hold this.

20:00.293 --> 20:01.598
"Congratulations.

20:01.632 --> 20:03.672
"You have won
The Founding Father Restaurant

20:03.707 --> 20:05.347
"Treasure Hunt Challenge.

20:05.381 --> 20:07.020
"Please enjoy one free meal

20:07.054 --> 20:09.296
"at select
Founding Father locations.

20:09.330 --> 20:11.773
Expires May 16, 2006."

20:11.807 --> 20:13.547
Wait a second.
What year is it?

20:13.582 --> 20:15.389
It's 2013, Peter.

20:15.423 --> 20:16.962
So that's...
It's before.

20:16.996 --> 20:18.200
The coupon's no good.

20:18.235 --> 20:19.539
Oh, man!

20:19.573 --> 20:21.882
Um, this sucks worse

20:21.917 --> 20:24.560
than when I went
to that strip club without Lois.

20:24.594 --> 20:25.397
(dance beat thumping,
men whooping)

20:25.432 --> 20:27.405
Yay!

20:31.443 --> 20:33.602
Well, Peter, I hope
you're not disappointed

20:33.603 --> 20:34.774
we didn't find
any treasure.

20:34.808 --> 20:35.978
No, it's fine.

20:36.013 --> 20:37.385
You know, the important thing is

20:37.419 --> 20:39.259
we figured out
those clues together.

20:39.294 --> 20:41.334
I mean, so what
we won't be able to pay

20:41.369 --> 20:42.840
to fix them veins
in your legs.

20:42.875 --> 20:44.447
You're my treasure, Lois,

20:44.481 --> 20:47.192
and I want you
on my team for everything.

20:47.226 --> 20:48.865
Except for sports.

20:48.901 --> 20:50.238
Me too, Peter.

20:50.273 --> 20:51.444
I love you.

20:51.478 --> 20:53.485
I love you, too, Lois.

20:53.519 --> 20:56.230
(knocking on door)
No way that's the shrimp.

20:56.231 --> 21:57.231
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru